  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-7-PPR-4000007219</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnership for improving prospects for forcibly displaced and host communities, UNHCR phase II contribution.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Second Phase of the MFA&apos;s Partnership with IFC, ILO, UNHCR, UNICEF and the World Bank to improve prospects for forcibly displaced and their host communities by together pushing for a transformation from taking a humanitarian to a development approach towards forced displacement. The 5 partners will push this transformation by focusing on the nexuses between, education, protection, employment, and critical infrastructure (housing, wash, connectivity. The partnership has been rolled out in 8 countries: Iraq, Jordan, Lebanon, Egypt, Sudan, Ethiopia, Kenya and Uganda. This Activity appraisal document will highlight the second phase of this Partnership and the specific role and activities of UNHCR under this Partnership, which will be funded by the MFA.</narrative>
  </description>
